  "summary_en": "2016 Citi GPS and Oxford Martin School report on automation's labour-market effects. It extends the Frey-Osborne 47% US job-risk estimate to other countries and cities, and covers productivity, inflation, sector impacts and barriers to automation. It recommends education, retraining and labour-market policies. Robot regulation is only a minor theme.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "47% of US jobs and higher shares in China (77%) and India (69%) are susceptible to automation.",
   "Creative intelligence, social intelligence, and perception and manipulation are the three bottlenecks to automation.",
   "Falling robot payback periods are lowering economic barriers to automation.",
   "Recommends education investment, retraining, EITCs and active labour-market policies over basic income.",
   "Developing countries risk premature deindustrialisation and need to upskill their workforces."
